  <running_head>EVANGELI. SECULI. V.</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">selegit. Huius sanctitatis respectu A-</l>
    <l n="2">postolus liberos Corinthiorum vocat</l>
    <l n="3">Sanctos, 1. Cor. 7: 14. Qui sanctitate</l>
    <l n="4">federali sanctus est opponitur βεβήλῳ</l>
    <l n="5">profano, qui extra fedus Dei est, &amp; ad</l>
    <l n="6">ecclesiam non spectat. Secunda est</l>
    <l n="7">
      <i>sanctitas sacramentalis</i>, quâ per baptis-</l>
    <l n="8">mum foederatis externâ aquæ aspersio-</l>
    <l n="9">ne remissio peccatorum per sanguinem</l>
    <l n="10">Christi &amp; regeneratio per Spiritum</l>
    <l n="11">sanctum, item per usum Eucharistiæ</l>
    <l n="12">participatio corporis &amp; sanguinis Chri-</l>
    <l n="13">sti obsignatur. Hæc superiore illa stri-</l>
    <l n="14">ctior est, reprobis tamen quoque com-</l>
    <l n="15">petit, cuius obsignationis respectu di-</l>
    <l n="16">cuntur ab Apostolo Paulo <i>illuminati</i>,</l>
    <l n="17">&amp; per Christi sanguinem <i>sanctificati</i>,</l>
    <l n="18">adeò, ut hisce mediis abutentes, dican-</l>
    <l n="19">tur Filium Dei conculcare &amp; sangui-</l>
    <l n="20">nem foederis, per quem fuerant (sacra-</l>
    <l n="21">mentali sanctitate) sanctificati, profa-</l>
    <l n="22">nare, Spiritumque gratiæ (obsignatæ)</l>
    <l n="23">contumeliâ afficere, Heb. 10: 29. Tertia</l>
    <l n="24">est <i>sanctitas spiritualis &amp; interna regene-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="25">
      <i>rationis</i>,</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Catchword and signature: "S 5" at the foot, read as a gathering signature. Some words in the Greek are uncertain; the Greek "βεβήλῳ" is transcribed as printed. The last line runs into a catchword "regene-" which is part of the text.</notes>
